+ * BIT(27); BIT(31) more is the interrupting kind, which this polling wait does not ask
+ * for), and Linux's a7xx_submit builds the same. WRITE_SRC 0 is the payload word after the
+ * 64-bit address (EV_WRITE_USER_32B), WRITE_DST 0 is memory (EV_DST_RAM): with the bit off
+ * the core writes nothing anywhere, and the submission number a waiter reads in the scratch
+ * page never arrives -- the sixth generation's event word (0x04) asked for the event alone
+ * and put the number in a scratch register instead.
